## Environment parity

- Every developer should run three commands and have the full app: `npm install`, `docker-compose up`, `npm run dev`
- LocalStack emulates S3 in dev so no AWS account needed to build
- Clerk works identically in dev and prod (dev instance keys vs prod instance keys)
- Prod config diverges only in env vars pointing at real AWS + Clerk prod instance

## HIPAA stance

This is not HIPAA-certified. It is HIPAA-architected. Acknowledge clearly in README.

In place:
- HIPAA-eligible AWS services only
- Encryption at rest (S3 KMS, RDS storage encryption)
- Encryption in transit (TLS 1.2+)
- Signed single-use tokens for patient access
- Append-only audit log
- Least-privilege IAM
- Rate limiting, helmet, CORS with specific origins
- Secrets in env vars (Secrets Manager in prod)

Not in place (would need for prod):
- BAA with AWS and Clerk (or migration to self-hosted auth)
- SOC 2 audit
- Intrusion detection
- Formal breach procedures
- Employee HIPAA training

